            <ArticleTitle>The effects of beta blockers on exercise capacity and on training response in elderly subjects.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>117-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Treatment of 8 hypertensive elderly subjects with atenolol or with labetalol did not affect exercise performance, except after the development of circulatory congestion in 1 patient. Treatment with beta blockers did not alter the response to an exercise training programme in 15 elderly patients with ischaemic heart disease, as compared with 11 patients without such treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
